From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 17:34:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 04/78] is_range_test: do not treat a constant as the tested
 variable

After inlining with constant arguments '(3 <= 0) or (1 <= 0)' reaches
the range-test transformation before the comparisons are folded; the
constant 0 was taken as the variable and the expression folded to True.
---
 compiler/nadd.pas | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/compiler/nadd.pas b/compiler/nadd.pas
index 7d60e94e..8d77d9ed 100644
--- a/compiler/nadd.pas
+++ b/compiler/nadd.pas
@@ -455,6 +455,11 @@ const
           if not value.isequal(valuer) then
             exit;
 
+          { both sides constant: nothing to range-test (and treating the
+            constant as "the variable" gives wrong results) }
+          if is_constnode(value) then
+            exit;
+
           { This is based on De Morgan's theorem, namely that
             "A and B" = "not ((not A) or (not B))" }
           inverted_range:=(nodetype=orn);
